  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Slalom around the rink",
  "description": "The players stand in a line, each with a puck. The first skates at high speed with the puck through a slalom along one board, around the far end and back through a tighter row of low cones along the other board. The next player starts once the one ahead has passed a few cones.\n\nGo around high cones wide, with body, stick and puck all on the outside. Set low cones closer together for short, quick puck moves. With lots of players, run two lines at once. Switch direction so the players turn both ways, or add a shot at the end. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Lean into the turn and take your whole body around the cone."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Short strides in the turns, long strides on the straights."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Keep the puck close to the blade – look up between the cones."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Do not start until the player ahead is up to speed."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
